# Full Reindex Realm

## Summary
Host command — force a full realm reindex. This republishes a from-scratch indexing job after clearing indexed mtimes, so every file in the realm is revisited even if mtimes have not changed. Use this when the user suspects indexing drift, stale cached results, or wants a full rebuild instead of the lighter default reindex. A user may request that they want to perform a full or deep reload/refresh of a realm in order to fully reindex it.. Available to
cards and commands via the runtime loader, and to AI assistant rooms as a
tool.

## Example
```ts
import FullReindexRealmTool from '@cardstack/boxel-host/commands/full-reindex-realm';

let result = await new FullReindexRealmTool(commandContext).execute({
  /* input fields */
} as any);
```
`commandContext` comes from `@context.commandContext` inside any card
format. In an AI room the same tool is invoked by name (action verb: Full Reindex).
